  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "For example, some people use Quest 2\\3\\Pro handtracking in PCVR version of VRC, and to be able to move somehow, they use some sorts of bluetooth controllers (like dualshock 4). But the problem is that doing that results in avatar hands switching to default position, as is \"vr controllers\" are put away (but they don't, because hands position are used).\n\nTwo times I was able to ignore that behavior in VirtualDesktop by:\n\n1)Going into passthrough\n\n2)Taking battery from right controller\n\n3)Taking battery from left controller, while holding trigger button (the possibility that it is needed to be held before going into passthrough)\n\n4)Quest enables hand tracking\n\n5)Going out of passthrough\n\n6)Moving using any other controller, while seeing that hands doesn't go into default position.\n\nMy point that I want VRC to have option to ignore that behavior, that allowing to not suffer from hand-less experience.\n\nIf needed, I can add video where it is shown in 6).",
